// GUARDIAN DUEL, the TypeScript port of the deterministic C# engine
// `CosQuest.Duel` (costquest-duel). Android plays Quest Point fights on this;
// iOS runs the same rules in Unity. The port is bit-exact: the same setup and
// inputs give the same state and the same 64-bit Hash() as the C# engine, so
// the server's replay verifier (C#) can check an Android fight. That is proven
// by __tests__/golden.json, generated by the real engine (scripts/duel-golden).
// No React or React Native here: it runs in Hermes and under `node --test`.
//
// HOW TO USE IT (one fight):
//
//   1. Start: POST /v1/duel/start. Keep the seed exact: it is a 62-bit integer
//      that JSON.parse rounds. features/game/client.ts parseDuelStart gives
//      `seed_text`; pass it along:
//        const setup = setupFromServer(start.setup, start.seed_text);
//        const view = presentationFromServer(start.setup);   // names, factions, levels
//      (setupFromServer also takes the raw setup JSON text and parses it exactly.)
//
//   2. Input: one GestureRecognizer over the fight area.
//        const g = new GestureRecognizer({ width, height });
//        onTouchStart  -> g.press(t, x, y, id)     (t in ms, e.g. performance.now())
//        onTouchMove   -> g.move(t, x, y, id)
//        onTouchEnd    -> g.release(t, x, y, id)  (cancel -> g.cancel(t))
//        special buttons -> g.special(1) / g.special(2)
//
//   3. Loop: a DuelRunner steps the sim at a fixed 60 Hz from real time.
//        const runner = new DuelRunner(setup, { input: g });
//        every frame: g.poll(now); const r = runner.advance(now - last);
//                     play r.events; draw runner.sim.state (runner.drawX(side) to interpolate)
//      Show a VS card / countdown before the first advance (the sim waits).
//      Hit-stop: while state.hitStop > 0 the fight and the clock are frozen;
//      hold both fighters' poses.
//
//   4. Finish: once runner.over, POST /v1/duel/finish with device_key, duel_id
//      and runner.finishPayload():
//        { result: { winner, ticks, p1_hp, p2_hp }, inputs: [[tick, code] | [tick, code, run]], hash: "16 hex" }
//
// WHAT TO DRAW (runner.sim.state: DuelState):
//   tick, ticksLeft (round clock, 60 per second), hitStop, over, winner (1, 2, 0 draw), endReason
//   p1 / p2 (FighterState): x (mm from the arena centre, +x right; the arena is
//   setup.arenaHalfWidthMm each side), facing (+1 right), action (FighterAction,
//   one animation each) with actionTick / actionLength for normalised time,
//   actionStartup, move (MoveId), hp / stats.maxHp, meter (0-300, three bars),
//   guard (0-100), hitStop, holding, chargeTicks (heavy glow), comboStep,
//   invulnerable, inActiveFrames.
// Events (DuelEvent: type, tick, source/target side 1|2, move, damage, hitStop,
// x mm): Hit, Blocked, GuardBreak, Knockdown, Telegraph, SpecialStart,
// DodgeStart, DashStart, KO, Timeout.
//
// Wire codes (InputKind): 1 Tap, 2 SwipeToward, 3 SwipeAway, 4 HoldStart,
// 5 HoldEnd, 6 Special1, 7 Special2, 8 MoveToward, 9 MoveAway (only 8 and 9
// may be runs). 0 None is never sent.

